# The sbt launcher drops its own default JAVA_OPTS once this file exists, so
# the encoding it would have set has to be repeated here.
-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8

# JDK 24 turned both of these into warnings printed before sbt says hello.
# sbt's own Scala library reaches for sun.misc.Unsafe in `scala.runtime.LazyVals`,
# and sbt loads JNA's native library through `System.load`. Neither is ours to
# fix, and neither is a problem yet, so say so up front rather than reading the
# same eight lines on every boot.
--sun-misc-unsafe-memory-access=allow
--enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED
